# OzoneAI — Agent rules

Follow `docs/architecture/tech-stack.md` and `docs/requirements/v3/` as source of truth.

## Stack (do not substitute without an explicit product decision)

- API: ASP.NET Core 9, Clean Architecture (`Domain` / `Application` / `Infrastructure` / `Api`), MediatR + FluentValidation
- Admin UI: React + TypeScript (Vite) + Ant Design + AG Grid in `apps/ozone_web`
- Mobile: Flutter flavors (customer / sales / van) in `apps/ozone_mobile`
- DB: PostgreSQL — one DB per company (`ozone_t_{key}`) + central `ozone_catalog`; pgvector for embeddings
- Search: Meilisearch (self-hosted Docker)
- Cache/jobs: Redis + Hangfire
- Storage: MinIO (S3 API)
- AI: Semantic Kernel + Ollama / OpenAI-compatible — propose-only, never auto-post ledgers
- Deploy: Docker Compose; open source / self-hosted — **no Azure**

## Workflow

- One Linear issue per branch: `feat/OZC-xxx-short-name` (or `feat/e1-1-short-name` until Linear IDs exist)
- PR target: `develop`; never force-push `main`
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, keys, connection strings with real passwords)

## Code style

- Match existing project patterns; prefer minimal diffs
- Tenant isolation is mandatory — never query another company's DB without audited impersonation
- Specs live under `docs/requirements/v3/`; link the spec path in PRs
